Under `--type-system-refresh`, the witness of a newtype declared without a constraint variable (such as `newtype N = int witness 1 + 1`, or a newtype over an arrow type) is checked for underspecified types with the rest of the declarations, so a Debug build no longer fails an assertion in `BinaryExpr.ResolvedOp` on an operator in it, and an underspecified witness is reported as an error instead of failing a cast. A Release build reports and verifies the same as before.
